    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10883": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Student Assistant – Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Student Assistant – Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Assistant – Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01094 Position Title Student Assistant – Clinical Psychology Department Academic Affairs: Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology Position Summary The Student Assistant – Clinical Psychology will provide administrative support to the Program Director, Director of Clinical Training, and core faculty in the Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.) program. Responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: clerical assistance (copying, scanning, filing, organizing, scheduling, and drafting email correspondence); administrative support (maintaining databases to support practicum activities, collecting and organizing academic and practicum data, maintaining program test library, communicating with internal and external constituencies to assist practicum placements, editing departmental manuals, forms, and brochures); assisting with recruitment, admission, interview and orientation processes; and coordinating departmental events. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially with Federal work study eligibility.  Current Psychology or Counseling and Human Services major with a cumulative GPA of 3.0 or above preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to maintain confidentiality and to maintain appropriate professional boundaries Excellent time management skills High level of organization and ability to attend to detail and meet deadlines Self-motivated and able to work independently as appropriate with administrative projects Ability to multitask, pay strict attention to detail, and meet deadlines Ability to interact with external audiences, such as potential new students or clinical supervisors at practicum sites Flexible and able to work independently and as part of a team Open to supervision and responsive to corrective feedback Commit to an assigned schedule of up to 20 hours per week during the academic semester on the Greenspring campus. Physical Requirements Medium work: exerting up to 40 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Requires physical abilities consistent with a busy college environment on a campus with buildings separated by some distance. Daily work with computers, monitors, copy machines, and other office equipment is required. Keyboarding, standing and/or sitting, walking, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal. Essential Functions Carry out clerical duties such as copying, scanning, ordering, filing, organizing, scheduling, and drafting correspondence, reports, and other program documents. Assist with maintaining, monitoring and updating the program’s practicum database and related records. Assist with checking items in and out of the program’s test library and maintaining inventory of test materials. Assist with collecting and organizing academic and practicum data. Assist with communicating with internal and external constituencies via phone, mail, email, and/or face-to-face communication to assist practicum placements and other departmental projects. Assist with setting up, coordinating, and marketing/publicizing departmental events. Assist with maintaining, updating, and distributing departmental manuals, forms, and brochures. Assist with coordination of details for departmental programs or special events, departmental meetings and seminars, etc. Assist with recruitment, admission, interview and orientation processes. Assist with planning meetings, scheduling appointments, making meeting arrangements, and maintaining documentation of meeting content. Gather and compile data in order to generate reports as required to support accreditation processes. Reports To Graduate Program Director, Psychology Posting Information Number of Available Positions 1 Work Location Greenspring Position Category Student Position Type Student Employee Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week up to 20 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 02/03/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
