    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10022": {
      "title": "Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work.",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Van Driver (Non CDL) Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Van Driver (Non CDL) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201200992P Position Title Van Driver (Non CDL) Department Campus Safety: Transportation Position Summary Operate University vehicles to provide safe transportation of faculty, staff, students and guests to on and off campus locations as assigned. Education/Experience High School Diploma plus two years commercial, professional driving experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Valid driver’s license along with a good driving record, and must be insurable. Must be drug free and pass random drug tests as required by the Department of Transportation Knowledge/Skills/Ability Ability to safely operate multi passenger vehicle in strict compliance with State regulations while maintaining professional courtesy with all passengers. Ability to write detailed and accurate reports. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Ability to understand and follow safety procedures and make logical decisions. Ability to detect problems and report information to appropriate personnel. Ability to operate equipment safely, such as vehicle wheelchair lift and two-way radios. Operate a wheelchair lift, load and unload passengers on and off the bus. Assure seatbelts and securing devices are fastened when positioning wheelchairs in the bus. Possess strong interpersonal skills, which include courtesy, politeness, and the ability to successfully interact with different cultures and personalities in a professional and tactful manner. Ability to gather data, i.e. ridership counts, compile information and prepare reports. Basic knowledge of Hazardous Materials and Identification Plaques. Attends meetings, programs and in-service training as assigned. Required to complete First Aid, CPR , AED , Blood borne Pathogen, and other courses required by the University. Maintain current required licenses and endorsements. Ability to send and receive electronic communications, i.e. Email Ability to be available to work on weekends, early mornings, and nights. Physical Requirements Light work, exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Climbing, crouching, standing, walking, lifting, talking, hearing. Visual acuity is required by Department of Transportation rules and regulations. Will be required to work in adverse weather conditions. Will be required to sit and drive for long periods and comply with DOT regulations. Required to safely and carefully operate University buses or other vehicles for long periods of time and during inclement weather in compliance with DOT regulations. Subject to inside and outside environmental conditions; subject to occasional extreme heat and cold. Essential Functions Operate University vehicles to provide safe transportation of faculty, staff, students and guests to on and off campus locations as assigned. Perform vehicle pre-trip and post-trip inspections, reporting any defects. Build rapport with students and employees Must respect all passengers. Maintain a clean and neat vehicle. Assures maintenance of bus in a safe and clean operating condition; reporting needed mechanical repairs, sweeping the interior of the bus, washing the windows, service the bus with gas and oil, follows established security procedures. Inspects the condition of the bus daily and reports all damage. Report, within 24 hours, when Driver’s license status has been affected by suspension, revocation, cancellation, lost privilege or disqualification. Must notify superior of any conviction of any type of Motor Vehicle State or local law relating to vehicle control as occurred. Also, report any parking violations issued involving a University Vehicle while in the driver’s control. Complete Found Property reports for any items left in vehicle. Complete rider logs for all persons transported and uses two-way-radio to communicate with the security office at the Owings Mills Campus. Assist Campus Security Officers by communicating via handheld radio suspicious or criminal activity on observed on or near campus. May be asked to work at Special events; i.e. athletic games, theatre events, commencements etc., to assist security officers with traffic and crowd control/management while under the direction of security personnel and notifying security of any circumstance needing Campus security consideration. Must report any circumstance that would affect compromise or impair the ability to perform the essential functions of this position. Reports To Transportation Supervisor Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/7177 Posting Information Number of Available Positions 1 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Staff Position Type Part-Time On-Call Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week up to 40 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 01/10/2022 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you possess a valid Driver's License? Yes No Are you available to work evenings and weekends? (Open Ended Question) Are you available to work holidays? Yes No How many hours per week are you available to work? 0 - 5 6 - 10 11 - 15 16 - 20 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
