      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Career Connection Center",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Career Connection Center Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study – Assistant Career Connection Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For summer 2026 Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01107 Position Title Work Study – Assistant Career Connection Center Department Career Connection Center Position Summary Student Assistant will provide administrative and receptionist support. Responsibilities will include but not be limited to answering phone calls for the Career Connection Center ( CCC ), greeting guests to the office, assist with student intake appointments, and general administrative support. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially with Federal work study eligibility. Must have at least a 2.5 GPA . Customer service experience preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Excellent grammar and spelling Excellent customer service skills Ability to handle multiple interruptions Good work ethic and professionalism Have an ongoing knowledge of the services, events, and procedures in the Career Connection Center. Must commit to an assigned schedule of 8-12 hours per week during the academic semester Interest in helping others and working with students, staff, employers, and faculty Articulate, with excellent communication skills Ability to use tact and diplomacy in working with others, both face to face and on the phone Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite, preferred Detail oriented, dependable and reliable; initiative and enthusiasm Ability to work evenings Physical Requirements Light work: exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Keyboarding, standing and/or sitting, walking, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal. Essential Functions Answer phone calls and direct calls to the appropriate staff member Assist students visiting the CCC for the first time via Student Intake Appointments. Help students schedule appointments with their designated Career Advisor Provide general office reception duties; greet student appointments as well as visiting employers. Work closely with Career Connection Center staff on special projects and events (e.g. administrative and paper management tasks; events and career fair prep, phone calls in support of First Destination Survey collection). Reports To Senior Career Advisor Posting Information Number of Available Positions 4 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 9-10 months Hrs/Week 8-12 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement Stevenson University is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you qualify for Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-