    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/9727": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Nursing (Laboratory)",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Nursing (Laboratory) Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study – Assistant Nursing (Laboratory) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Looking for a Federal Work Study Eligible student. Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01053 Position Title Work Study – Assistant Nursing (Laboratory) Department School of Nursing & Health Professions: Dean's Office Position Summary The Work Study – Assistant Nursing will provide support to the Director of Clinical Practice, Lab Manager, Lab Staff, Nursing Faculty, and/or students for the Nursing Skills Laboratory. Education/Experience Currently enrolled at Stevenson University and in good standing with the university both academically and judicially.   Junior or senior level nursing major preferred.  Healthcare experience/medical terminology knowledge required.  Experience in working in a healthcare environment preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Computer competency required to work in Microsoft Office, Blackboard, TracCloud, and internet applications such as web-based training EHR . Excellent organizational skills with attention to detail Excellent interpersonal, time management, and collaboration skills. Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Ability to be creative and resourceful Ability to maintain safety and hygiene standards. Ability to coordinate and implement assignments to meet faculty/student needs. Ability to positively interact with staff, students, and faculty. Knowledge and ability to use medical equipment (e.g. hospital beds, intravenous (IV) pumps, monitors, oxygen delivery systems, SIM pads, Pyxis etc.) Ability to operate a human patient simulator. Serve as a standardized patient for non-invasive simulation experiences. Physical Requirements Ability to lift up to 50 lbs., move, and carry a training mannequin and/or walk or stand for an extended period of time.  Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Requires physical abilities consistent with a busy college and/or clinical environment on a campus with buildings, laboratories, or other sites separated by some distance. Sitting, standing, walking, talking, hearing, keyboarding, and repetitive motions. Close visual acuity. Position requires sitting and standing for long periods of time. Essential Functions Assist with setting up campus skills laboratories for scheduled labs, practice, and skills validation sessions. Assist with breakdown, cleaning, and storage of small equipment and manikins utilized during demonstration, practice, and skills validation sessions. Maintain labs in a clean and orderly manner at all times. Maintain sign-in log and accurate documentation of student open lab hours. Assist in ordering and maintaining laboratory supplies, equipment, and inventory. Assist faculty with debriefing of simulation experiences. Reports To Work Study – Assistant Nursing (Laboratory) Posting Information Number of Available Positions 3 Work Location Owings Mills North Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 9- 12 Hrs/Week 10- 20 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 11/14/2023 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
