    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10670": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study - Assistant Residence Life",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study - Assistant Residence Life Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study - Assistant Residence Life Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01123 Position Title Work Study - Assistant Residence Life Department Student Affairs: Residence Life Position Summary This position is a critical “front-line” role for the Office of Residence Life and is responsible for providing good customer service. Student Assistants are expected to know, voice, model, and motivate students and guests to adhere to the policies and procedures of Stevenson University. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Must possess excellent organizational and communication skills, a willingness to accept responsibility, and an attention to detail. Have general knowledge of Microsoft Office applications, as well as e-mail, internet and phone operations. Ability to arrive for duty on time as assigned in order to maintain a staffed desk. Ability to work evenings and weekends as needed. Physical Requirements Light work: exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Keyboarding, standing and/or sitting, walking, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal. Essential Functions Provide general office reception duties; greet residents, staff, faculty, and visitors. Answer phone calls and forward to the appropriate staff member. Provide excellent customer service to residents, staff, and guests of the halls. Maintain the cleanliness and organization of the front desk. Answer the front desk phone and forward calls or take messages appropriately. Answer basic questions about residence life operations. Maintain logs for pertinent daily work Create basic documents using Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Perform general clerical duties such as filing, copying, etc. Perform customer service duties such as lock-outs, submitting maintenance requests, resident check-in, etc. Attend training sessions and meetings as determined by the Assistant Director, Housing Operations Perform other duties as assigned by your supervisor. Communicate policies and instructions correctly and respectfully to residents and guests. Receive and report requests for repairs, maintenance and lock changes Maintain accurate logs for lockouts, equipment check-out etc. Inventory and maintain equipment (i.e. cleaning supplies, games.) Distribute flyers to resident assistant mailboxes. Provide follow up for residents’ concerns Refer to Stevenson University Handbook and Stevenson Guidelines for Housing to accurately and appropriately answer questions. Reports To Assistant Director, Housing Operations Posting Information Number of Available Positions 10 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 10 Hrs/Week 10-20 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 08/26/2025 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
