      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Student Assistant - Theatre Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Assistant - Theatre Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply if you have any technical theatre, or construction experience Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01155 Position Title Student Assistant - Theatre Department School of Design, Arts, and Communication: Theatre Position Summary Assist the Technical Director in all aspects of theatrical production including set construction, lighting & sound and staffing for outside events using the Berman Family Performing Arts Center. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Know theatrical terminology Familiar with hand and power tools Previous experience with theatrical productions is a plus Physical Requirements Medium work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Activity includes keyboarding, standing and/or sitting, walking, lifting, climbing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, reaching, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal and reading printed materials. Subject to both environmental conditions; activities occur inside and outside. Essential Functions Assist the Technical Director on all performance aspects. Staffing outside events held in the theatre. Assist with box office during productions. Reports To Professor, Theatre and Tech Dir & Mgr, BPAC 