    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/9730": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant, Registrar’s Office",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant, Registrar’s Office Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study – Assistant, Registrar’s Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01063 Position Title Work Study – Assistant, Registrar’s Office Department Registrar's Office Position Summary The Work Study – Assistant, Registrar’s Office works as a member of a team to support the Office of the Registrar.  Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, performing general office and clerical tasks; assisting with events hosted by the Office of Registrar; answering phones; entering data; filing, scanning, typing, faxing, and copying documents. This position requires FERPA training, which is provided. Education/Experience Current enrolled student at Stevenson University in good standing with the University, academically and judicially, with Federal Work Study eligibility. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Organized with careful attention to detail and accuracy. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Exceptional interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint is desired. Database management and other computer skills are valued. Self-motivated, flexible, with a strong work ethic. Commitment to integrity, excellence, learning, and community. Ability to work a minimum of 10 hours per week. Complete FERPA training and maintain strict confidentiality regarding all aspects of the position. Physical Requirements Medium work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Standing and/or sitting, walking, keyboarding, talking and hearing is required. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal is required. Subject to inside and outside environmental conditions. Position may require additional hours for meetings and events.  Perform general clerical and office support functions that include, but are not limited to, filing, scanning, typing, faxing, running errands, and copying. Essential Functions Assist callers/visitors by providing general information. Assist with projects as assigned. Assist with events. Prepare materials or mailings. Assist with data entry. Reports To Assistant Registrar Posting Information Number of Available Positions 1 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week No more than 20 per week Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 02/19/2024 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you qualify for Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package? Yes No What days/times are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
