    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10720": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Student Assistant - Mailroom",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Student Assistant - Mailroom Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Assistant - Mailroom Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01082 Position Title Student Assistant - Mailroom Department Mail Services Position Summary The Student Assistant – Mailroom will participate in all facets of the Mailroom and Materials Management to include receipt and distribution of packages on multiple campuses as well as organization of the Materials storeroom. This position will work closely with the courier to provide support with the distribution of interoffice mail and packages while handling inbound freight deliveries. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially. Experience in mail distribution a plus but not required. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Good communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to liaison with external companies. Ability to work independently. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Experience with computers. Physical Requirements Medium work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or 50 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Activity includes keyboarding, standing and/or sitting, walking, lifting, climbing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, reaching, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal and reading printed materials. Subject to both environmental conditions; activities occur inside and outside. Essential Functions Assist the courier with all deliveries on both campuses. Arrange for pickup and delivery of freight and bulk packages. Liaison with Stevenson personnel. Arrange and monitor storage in Materials Management Arrange and maintain the Avalon Center Mailroom. Reports To Manager Posting Information Number of Available Positions 2 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Student Position Type Student Employee Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week up to 10 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 10/06/2025 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
