    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/9737": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study - Assistant Fashion Design",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study - Assistant Fashion Design Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study - Assistant Fashion Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01087 Position Title Work Study - Assistant Fashion Design Department School of Design, Arts, and Communication: Fashion Design Position Summary This position will be responsible for assisting the Program Coordinator, Studio Manager, faculty, staff, and students during scheduled classes and Open Studio periods with their course-related technical fashion design projects. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University, both academically and judicially Fashion Design major with at least a 3.0 GPA . Junior status, and previous technical fashion design experience preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Ability to work at least 7.5 hours per week during the academic semester. Proficient in clothing construction, flat patternmaking, draping, tailoring, and the operation of sewing and pressing equipment. Ability to guide the fashion design students in executing their technical fashion design projects. Ability to work effectively with the faculty, professional staff, and peers in the Fashion Design program. Ability to assist the instructors during scheduled technical fashion design classes during the day and evening. Ability to work independently and supervise Open Studio periods for students during the day. Ability to read, listen, and communicate information and ideas through spoken and written language. Ability to use various means of communication (e.g. telephone, computer, other electronic devices) to work with students, peers, and outside contacts. Must be organized, dedicated, punctual, responsible, and detail-oriented. Must have excellent time management skills and be ability to work under pressure. Physical Requirements Medium work: exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Fingering, standing and/or sitting, walking, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing and using industrial equipment. Essential Functions Assist the students during selected classes and Open Studio periods. Provide support to the faculty and the staff by assisting with technical work related to the academic program. Assist the students during scheduled technical fashion design classes. Work independently and assist with the day-to-day operation of the fashion design studio. Reports To Studio Manager Posting Information Number of Available Positions Varies Work Location Owings Mills North Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week No more than 20 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 08/16/2024 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you qualify for Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
