    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11031": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Maintenance Technician Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Maintenance Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a posting for those interested in being included in the applicant pool for this position. There is no guarantee that the University is actively hiring for an open position at this time. Should a position be available and a review of your qualifications results in a decision to pursue your candidacy, the hiring manager will contact you. Your application will remain active in the pool until the posting is closed. Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201201377P Position Title Maintenance Technician Department Facility Services: Owings Mills Position Summary Under general supervision, performs a broad range of semi-skilled tasks and maintenance duties in the building construction and maintenance field. Including, but not limited to, HVAC , plumbing, electrical, carpentry, appliance repair, and painting. Assist in Snow removal when necessary. Assist in emergency service in addition to routine work as directed. This position is considered essential personnel. Education/Experience High school diploma plus three years’ work related experience in general maintenance field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Valid driver license and a good driving record; must be insurable. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Working knowledge and usage of hand and power tools associated with the maintenance field. Working knowledge of HVAC , plumbing, electrical, carpentry, painting repairs and installation as needed. Working knowledge of a computer generated work ticket system. Ability to practice effective verbal communication skills with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to read, understand and abide by all safety policies and procedures. Ability to work any assigned shift/work schedule. Available to be on-call at minimum of one week out of every four weeks. Ability to work 24/7 as the position requires. Physical Requirements Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Talking, hearing, climbing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, standing, walking, lifting, reaching, pushing, pulling, keyboarding, and grasping. Visual acuity to perform an activity such as operations of machines; using measurement devices; and/or visual inspections of small parts or devices. Subject to both environmental conditions. Activities occur inside and outside. Subject to hazards, noise, extreme cold and oils. Essential Functions Perform routine scheduled and unscheduled maintenance on air conditioning, heating, ventilation, refrigeration and other equipment/systems. Respond to all related repair requests and troubleshoots problems; making necessary repairs. Have a working knowledge of various HVAC controls. Perform routine and emergency repairs to basic plumbing fixtures, pipes and fittings duties. Perform minor routine and emergency repairs to electrical system components, including but not limited to, light fixtures, ballasts, switches and other electrical items. Perform minor repairs to grounds construction, including but not limited to roadways, walkways, interior and exterior walls, ceilings floors and other building surfaces. Assist with painting and general carpentry. Perform minor equipment and appliance repairs. Maintain and inspect assigned zone. Maintain the highest level of employee/guest relations Assist with event set-up and breakdown. Assist with snow removal. Reports To Director, Facilities Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10151 Posting Information Number of Available Positions 1 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Staff Position Type Full-Time Months/Year 12 Hrs/Week 40 Hrs/Year 2080 If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $20.00 to $21.60 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 03/19/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11248": {
      "title": "Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work.",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty, Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Criminal Justice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. *This position requires teaching in-person classes at Stevenson University in Owings Mills, MD. This position is part of a bargaining unit represented by SEIU, Local 500, and the terms and conditions of employment will be governed by the terms of a Collective Bargaining Agreement between the University and the SEIU that is now being negotiated. This is a posting for those interested in being included in the applicant pool for this position. Should a position be available, and a review of your qualifications results in a decision to pursue your candidacy, the hiring manager will contact you directly. Your application will remain active in the pool until the posting is closed. Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201201518P Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Criminal Justice Department School of Humanities & Social Sciences: Criminal Justice Position Summary Adjunct faculty at Stevenson University will engage in teaching activities in accordance with the University’s faculty workload policies. Teaching responsibilities will include teaching courses in the School of Humanities & Social Sciences: Criminal Justice Department. Education/Experience Master’s degree in criminal justice or a closely related field from an accredited institution and three years of Criminal Justice experience in a practical setting, or equivalent combination of education and experience. Doctorate degree preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability · Knowledge of and/or experience working in the criminal justice system. · Demonstrated teaching ability in criminal justice. · Ability to instruct students of varying preparation and abilities. · Excellent interpersonal and cultural competency skills and demonstrated ability to communicate professionally with diverse constituencies. · Ability to create inclusive learning experiences that will help undergraduate students to develop professionally, intellectually, and socially. · Ability to work with students of diverse backgrounds and practice inclusive pedagogy. · Demonstrated student-centered approach to teaching, and a commitment to student achievement. · Ability to assess student performance and learning. · Proficiency in Microsoft applications, including PowerPoint, Word, Excel and Outlook. · Familiarity with educational assessment practices · Commitment to integrity, excellence, learning, and community. · Experience working with Blackboard or a similar learning management system. · Well-developed organizational, reasoning, and problem-solving skills. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. · Ability to manage time effectively and meet deadlines. · Ability to work effectively with colleagues. · Ability to travel between campuses. · Ability to work evenings and weekends, as needed. Physical Requirements Light work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Sitting, standing, walking, talking, hearing, keyboarding, and repetitive motions. Close visual acuity. Position requires sitting and standing for extended periods of time and the ability to speak clearly and effectively for an extended period of time. Essential Functions · Engage in instructional activity totaling no more than 18 contact hours per academic year (August through May), with no more than 9 contact hours taught in an individual semester. · Teaching responsibilities include time spent in the classroom, laboratory, or hybrid or online courses and in immediate preparation for them; maintaining competence in subjects being taught; preparing teaching materials; conferring with students on course materials; directing individual and group studies; reviewing written examinations and papers; evaluating presentations and projects; providing academic accommodations for students with documented disabilities. · Other responsibilities include writing syllabi; reading and responding to emails promptly; grading course work within a time frame that enables the student to incorporate feedback on their next assignment; timely submission of mid-term and final grades, attendance verification, academic alerts, and other reports as requested; and alerting appropriate university personnel to student problems on a timely basis. · Respond to student feedback for each course and complete training or professional development as required by the University. · Collegiality, as well as professional and ethical conduct, enhances teaching, learning and the general reputation of all persons in the academy. Therefore, all faculty members are expected to serve in a collegial fashion and in accordance with professional and ethical principles when dealing with other faculty members, students, administrators, and members of the public. Follow all faculty and program policies outlined by the School and the University. · Every faculty member is guaranteed academic freedom in accordance with the statement on academic freedom and responsibilities of faculty members, as set forth in the Stevenson University Policies. · Teaching assignments may require teaching day, evening, online or hybrid classes. · Meeting classes for the full class time during the scheduled dates and times is expected. Reports To Program Coordinator, Criminal Justice Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11056 Posting Information Number of Available Positions Varies as needed based on the needs of the department Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Faculty Position Type Adjunct Faculty Months/Year variable Hrs/Week variable Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Exempt Payroll Monthly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $1,191-$1,389 per credit/contact hour (subject to minimum enrollment) Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 04/15/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement Stevenson University is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to teach in-person classes at Stevenson University? Yes No * Do you have a Master's degree in criminal justice or criminology? Yes No * Do you have a Ph.D or Doctorate degree in criminal justice or a related field? Yes No * I understand that this posting is to create an applicant pool for this position and there is no guarantee that there is an open position at this time. My application will remain on file until the posting is closed. I understand and agree. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/10598": {
      "title": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Athletics (Student/Fan Engagement)",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Assistant Athletics (Student/Fan Engagement) Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study – Assistant Athletics (Student/Fan Engagement) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01112 Position Title Work Study – Assistant Athletics (Student/Fan Engagement) Department Athletics: Administrative Position Summary The Work Study – Assistant Athletics (Student/Fan Engagement) responsibilities include but are not limited to working different athletic events and providing support to the Associate Athletics Director in generating excitement, attendance and crowd engagement during home athletic events. Education/Experience Currently enrolled Stevenson University student in good standing with the University academically and judicially. Eligible for Federal Work-Study. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Punctuality and self-motivation are essential Must be dependable and reliable, a team player Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Preserving confidentiality is a must Customer service experience preferred. Ability to work in an independent environment. Excellent organizational skills Accuracy with attention to detail Capacity to multi-task and prioritize duties Knowledge in the use of Microsoft Office programs and other related computer applications. Ability to work evenings and weekends. Physical Requirements Medium work: Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds due to daily activities. Daily standing and/or sitting, walking, talking and hearing. Close visual acuity to perform an activity such as viewing a computer terminal. Subject to both environmental conditions; activities occur inside and outside in all types of weather. Essential Functions Assist in in all programs related to fan/student engagement at home athletic events. Athletic game day set-up and/or breakdown focusing on special events related to fan and student body engagement. Attend the Athletics Engagement Committee Meetings. Generate ideas to increase attendance at sporting events and increase crowd engagement. Assist in generating marketing materials for game day events. Work with Athletics Communications to communication special games through social media, flyers, Stevenson University Portal, etc. Work collaboratively with other student employees, athletics department staff and external sponsors. Provide game day support to effectively execute the fan engagement programs planned for that event. Work with the Athletics Engagement Committee to generate a calendar of events for the year, focusing on all sports, but primarily revenue generating sports. Reports To Associate Athletics Director Posting Information Number of Available Positions up to 10 Work Location Owings Mills Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 9 Hrs/Week up to 10 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date 08/24/2025 Ending Date 05/30/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 07/24/2025 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11118": {
      "title": "Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work.",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty, Physics Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Physics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is part of a bargaining unit represented by SEIU, Local 500, and the terms and conditions of employment will be governed by the terms of a Collective Bargaining Agreement between the University and the SEIU that is now being negotiated. This is a posting for those interested in being included in the applicant pool for this position. There is no guarantee that the University is actively hiring for an open position at this time. Should a position be available, and a review of your qualifications results in a decision to pursue your candidacy, the hiring manager will contact you directly. Your application will remain active in the pool until the posting is closed. Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201201520P Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Physics Department School of the Sciences: Engineering, Math & Physics Position Summary Adjunct faculty at Stevenson University will engage in teaching activities in accordance with the University’s faculty workload policies. Teaching responsibilities will include teaching courses in the Physics department. Education/Experience Master’s degree or doctorate in physics, a strong commitment to quality teaching, with college level teaching experience preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Knowledge of physics. Demonstrated teaching ability in physics. Ability to instruct students of varying preparation and abilities. Excellent interpersonal and cultural competency skills and demonstrated ability to communicate professionally with diverse constituencies. Ability to create inclusive learning experiences that will help graduate and/or undergraduate students to develop professionally, intellectually, and socially. Ability to work with students of diverse backgrounds and practice inclusive pedagogy. Demonstrated student-centered approach to teaching, and a commitment to student achievement. Ability to assess student performance and learning. Proficiency in Microsoft applications, including PowerPoint, Word, Excel and Outlook. Familiarity with educational assessment practices Commitment to integrity, excellence, learning, and community. Experience working with Blackboard or a similar learning management system. Well-developed organizational, reasoning, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to manage time effectively and meet deadlines. Ability to work effectively with colleagues. Ability to travel between campuses. Ability to work evenings and weekends, as needed. Physical Requirements Light work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Sitting, standing, walking, talking, hearing, keyboarding, and repetitive motions. Close visual acuity. Position requires sitting and standing for extended periods of time and the ability to speak clearly and effectively for an extended period of time. Subject to inside and outside environmental conditions. Science faculty work in science laboratories and will be exposed to chemicals, biologicals, chemical processes, magnetic field, and scientific equipment/instrumentation. Essential Functions Engage in instructional activity totaling no more than 18 contact hours per academic year (August through May), with no more than 9 contact hours taught in an individual semester. Teaching responsibilities include time spent in the classroom, laboratory, or hybrid or online courses and in immediate preparation for them; maintaining competence in subjects being taught; preparing teaching materials; conferring with students on course materials; directing individual and group studies; reviewing written examinations and papers; evaluating presentations and projects; providing academic accommodations for students with documented disabilities. Other responsibilities include writing syllabi; reading and responding to emails promptly; grading course work within a time frame that enables the student to incorporate feedback on their next assignment; timely submission of mid-term and final grades, attendance verification, academic alerts, and other reports as requested; and alerting appropriate university personnel to student problems on a timely basis. Respond to student feedback for each course and complete training or professional development as required by the University. Collegiality, as well as professional and ethical conduct, enhances teaching, learning and the general reputation of all persons in the academy. Therefore, all faculty members are expected to serve in a collegial fashion and in accordance with professional and ethical principles when dealing with other faculty members, students, administrators, and members of the public. Follow all faculty and program policies outlined by the School and the University. Every faculty member is guaranteed academic freedom in accordance with the statement on academic freedom and responsibilities of faculty members, as set forth in the Stevenson University Policies. Teaching assignments may require teaching day, evening, online or hybrid classes. Meeting classes for the full class time during the scheduled dates and times is expected. Reports To Department Chair Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11064 Posting Information Number of Available Positions Varies as needed based on the needs of the department Work Location Owings Mills North Position Category Faculty Position Type Adjunct Faculty Months/Year variable Hrs/Week variable Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Exempt Payroll Monthly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $1,191-$1,389 per credit/contact hour (subject to minimum enrollment) Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 04/29/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement Stevenson University is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree or a Ph.D.? Yes No * Please list any courses you have taught at the college level. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to teach in-person classes at Stevenson University? Yes No * Please indicate the hours you are available to teach courses (i.e.,daytime/evening, specific hours). (Open Ended Question) * I understand that this posting is to create an applicant pool for this position and there is no guarantee that there is an open position at this time. My application will remain on file until the posting is closed. I understand and agree. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
