    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11264": {
      "title": "Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work.",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Enrollment Counselor Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Enrollment Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a posting for those interested in being included in the applicant pool for this position. There is no guarantee that the University is actively hiring for an open position at this time. Should a position be available and a review of your qualifications results in a decision to pursue your candidacy, the hiring manager will contact you. Your application will remain active in the pool until the posting is closed. Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201201546P Position Title Enrollment Counselor Department Stevenson University Online: Admissions Position Summary The Enrollment Counselor (EC) is responsible for recruiting and enrolling qualified new students for Stevenson University Online ( SUO ) degree and certificate programs. The EC is assigned a portfolio of academic programs and is cross-trained to provide recruiting, admissions, and enrollment support for all SUO programs. This position requires strong interpersonal skills and a sales mindset, and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, contacting prospective students who have expressed an interest SUO programs; providing effective, regular, responsive, and proactive guidance to prospective students to support their enrollment in SUO ; representing SUO at recruitment events, fairs, and other related activities on-campus, off-campus, and virtually to generate student leads; maintaining professional relationships that support the generation of students leads and enrollment; and supporting the planning and execution of marketing, admissions, and other events related to SUO , including the Bachelor’s to Master’s option. Meeting established performance metrics is expected. The Enrollment Counselor tracks and collects relevant data and compiles regular and ad hoc reports as assigned. This position is campus-based and housed on the university’s Greenspring campus. The Enrollment Counselor works as a member of the team to support overall SUO operations and supports initiatives as requested. Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree required. Experience in higher education admissions preferred. Valid driver’s license with good driving record; must be insurable. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Demonstrated sales mindset and aptitude with well-developed ability to generate leads, pursue leads, and enroll students in academic programs. Ability to learn and maintain a current knowledge of application requirements and admission criteria for all SUO degree programs and certificates. Ability to function as a self-directed, highly motivated, high activity sales professional capable of meeting enrollment targets. Excellent interpersonal, cultural competency, teamwork, and networking skills and demonstrated ability to communicate professionally and effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to effectively present information and respond directly to questions asked by students and the general public in a group setting and/or on a one-to-one basis. Math aptitude is required to calculate mathematical problems such as discounts, interest, proportions, and percentages. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment, tact, and discretion, and to maintain confidentiality and integrity with handling sensitive and confidential information. Knowledge of rules, regulations, and laws regarding student records and ability to operate in accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act ( FERPA ). Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Excellent problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks under pressure and to adapt to rapidly changing priorities. Ability to organize offsite events, represent SUO at events, and enter leads for prospective students in the CRM system. Ability to effectively develop and provide sales presentations to relevant audiences. Ability to collect, organize, analyze, and report information. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications including, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, and Word, and ability to learn and use other software platforms that support SUO operations (e.g., Slate). Effectively interpret and follow instructions as given whether in written, oral, diagram, or other communication modality. Ability to properly handle and reasonably control any situation which may arise. Ability to work evenings and weekends. Regional and local travel is a requirement of this position. Physical Requirements Light work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Sitting standing, walking; talking; hearing; keyboarding and repetitive motions. Close visual acuity. Subject to inside environmental conditions. Essential Functions Learn and maintain current knowledge of SUO academic programs, activities, scholarships, partnerships, discounts, and other relevant information. Recruit, admit, and enroll prospective students in assigned portfolio of SUO’s academic programs to meet or exceed established performance metrics and goals. Provide excellent customer service to ensure student satisfaction throughout the recruitment, admission, and enrollment process. Generate prospective student leads by representing SUO at recruitment events, fairs, and other related activities held on-campus, off-campus, and/or virtually. Contact prospective students who have expressed an interest in SUO programs. Provide effective, regular, responsive, and proactive guidance to inquiries and prospective students to secure their completed application and subsequent enrollment in SUO . Review assigned student applications for admission, verify and evaluate credentials, and recommend admission decisions based on institutional guidelines. Track and collect relevant data and compile regular and ad hoc reports as assigned. In collaboration with the relevant academic program administrators and deans, plan and execute marketing, admissions, and other events related to the Bachelor’s to Master’s options. In collaboration with the relevant academic program administrators and deans, attend and assist in the planning, coordination, and hosting of recruiting events designed to meet the unique needs of online students, including information sessions, open houses, webinars, and other related events in support of SUO goals as requested. Facilitate seamless transition of accepted students to SUO Student Success Coach. Facilitate the circulation of relevant informational and promotional materials through all appropriate channels. Maintain an active contact database. Be creative in identifying and exploring new opportunities to enhance enrollment in SUO programs, and maintain professional relationships that support the generation of students leads and enrollment Cross-train and serve as position backup for recruiting, admitting, and enrolling prospective students in all of SUO’s academic programs. Assist with implementing marketing strategies (standard and e-marketing). Engage with the relevant academic program administrators and deans as requested to ensure alignment, currency, and accuracy of recruiting materials with academic programs. Maintain confidential records, collect data, and prepare reports as directed. Support SUO operations, events, and initiatives as assigned. Identify general SUO recruiting and admissions needs and share them with the Senior Director as possible opportunities for continuous improvement. Monitor inquiry, admission, and enrollment trends in assigned SUO programs, and report findings to Senior Director. Alert the Senior Director to any issues concerning transcript evaluation, financial aid, or other student concerns. Attend all School and University convocations and meetings. Maintain integrity when handling sensitive and confidential information in accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act ( FERPA ). Demonstrate professionalism when working with students and colleagues, effective multi-tasking and prioritization, adherence to deadlines, and flexibility. Reports To Senior Director, SUO Enrollment & Admissions Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11209 Posting Information Number of Available Positions Applicant Pool Work Location Greenspring Position Category Staff Position Type Full-Time Months/Year 12 Hrs/Week 40 Hrs/Year 2080 If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $45,000 to $47,500 Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability status, protected veteran status, genetics, or any other characteristic protected by law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I understand that this posting is to create an applicant pool for this position and there is no guarantee that there is an open position at this time. Please keep my application on file until the posting is closed. Yes. I understand and agree. No. I do not want my application to remain in the applicant pool. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/9729": {
      "title": "Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work.",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Work Study – Community Tutor Skip to Main Content Find Your Role:  We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Work Study – Community Tutor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 01062 Position Title Work Study – Community Tutor Department School of Education: Dean's Office Position Summary This student Work Study position will work in a nearby public school to support students in reading and mathematics. Education/Experience Current enrolled student at Stevenson University in good standing with the University, academically and judicially, with Federal Work Study eligibility. All majors are welcome to apply. Student must have at least a 2.5 GPA or higher. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Exceptional verbal and written communication skills. Ability to be a reliable and dependable worker with a positive attitude. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Excellent organizational skills. Ability to multi-task and work independently. Physical Requirements Light work: Exerting up to 25 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force constantly to move object.  Clear speaking voice. Stooping, kneeling, crouching, reaching, standing, walking, lifting, keyboarding, talking, hearing and repetitive motions. Essential Functions Provide support to elementary age children with reading and math in the classroom. Provide support to teachers as needed. Positively promote and represent Stevenson University as an Educational professional. Communicate professionally with students, school staff, teachers, and school leadership. Reports To Assistant to the Associate VP, Academic Affairs Posting Information Number of Available Positions 5 Work Location Other Position Category Student Position Type Student Work-Study Months/Year 6 Hrs/Week 10-15 Hrs/Year If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Non-Exempt Payroll Biweekly Hiring Salary Range $15.00 per hour Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Current Students Posting Date 02/20/2024 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement EOE /AA Employer of Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disability Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you qualify for Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package? Yes No Do you have your own reliable transportation? Yes No Do you have experience working with elementary, middle school, or high school students? Please describe. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
